​The report concludes that while there is much progress to be made in understanding how the energy industry affects various aspects of life in Texas, the results so far have been mixed and suggest that further research and study is needed. The report recommends that Texas agencies and organizations consider the following actions:
Establish a process for tracking and monitoring all potential impacts on health, safety, and quality of life for people living near oil and gas operations;
Develop and implement mitigation plans for communities affected by shale development;
Identify key data sources that would allow researchers to monitor long-term changes;
Include members of affected communities in any assessment or decision-making processes related to shale development;
Improve the ability of scientists to measure and analyze the full suite of potential impacts of shale development; and
Develop a systematic approach to studying and responding to the complex interactions between the energy industry and other parts of society.

The following code is an example implementation of a Redis client using nodejs:

var redis = require("redis");

class RedisClient {
    constructor(host, port) {
        var self = this;
        if (!host || !port) throw new Error("Missing host or port!");

        this.client = redis.createClient();
        this.client.on("error", function(err) {
            console.log("Error: " + err);
        });
        this.client.on("ready", function() {
            console.log("Redis ready!");
        });
        this.client.on("message", function(channel, message) {
            if (self.get) {
                self.get(channel, message).then(function(value) {
                    console.log("Got: " + value);
                }).catch(function(e) {
                    console.log("Error: " + e);
                });
            } else {
                self.set(channel, message).then(function(value) {
                    console.log("Set: " + value);
                }).catch(function(e) {
                    console.log("Error: " + e);
                });
            }
        });
    }
}

